CALLed programs
  ok      step over CALL does not enter the called program
  ok      step into CALL enters the called program
  ok      step over GOBACK returns to the calling program
  ok      step over a PERFORM in a called program stays in that program
  ok      the call stack shows the called program above the calling one
  BUG?    the call stack shows the CALL statement in the calling program
            -> frames: callee_ (ADD 10 TO N.)@8, callee@0, caller_@0, caller@0, main@0
  BUG?    breakpoint on GOBACK is hit
            -> the program terminated instead of stopping
  BUG?    step out of a called program returns to the calling program
            -> the program terminated instead of stopping
  BUG?    breakpoints in several source files are all hit
            -> first stop: expected callee.cbl:12, got caller.cbl:9
  BUG?    changing breakpoints in a file keeps those of other files
            -> first stop: expected callee.cbl:12, got caller.cbl:9
  BUG?    LINKAGE items of the called program show the passed data
            -> no variable N (have: RETURN-CODE)
  BUG?    the call stack only shows COBOL programs
            -> non-COBOL frames: callee, caller_, caller, main
